      "text": "EGD AND COLONOSCOPY REPORT"
    },
    {
      "id": "P2",
      "text": "Date of service: November 2, 2026"
    },
    {
      "id": "P3",
      "text": "Endoscopist: Adaeze Montclair, MD (fictional)"
    },
    {
      "id": "P4",
      "text": "Indication: Iron deficiency anemia."
    },
    {
      "id": "P5",
      "text": "EGD: The gastroscope was advanced to the second portion of the duodenum."
    },
    {
      "id": "P6",
      "text": "EGD findings: normal esophagus; mild antral erythema; mildly scalloped duodenal folds."
    },
    {
      "id": "P7",
      "text": "EGD biopsies: cold forceps biopsies of the second portion of the duodenum for celiac disease."
    },
    {
      "id": "P8",
      "text": "Cold forceps biopsies of the gastric antrum were also taken for Helicobacter pylori."
    },
    {
      "id": "P9",
      "text": "Colonoscopy: The colonoscope was then advanced to the cecum; the appendiceal orifice was seen."
    },
    {
      "id": "P10",
      "text": "Colonoscopy findings: a 2 cm patch of erythema in the sigmoid colon; otherwise normal."
    },
    {
      "id": "P11",
      "text": "Colonoscopy biopsy: cold forceps biopsies were taken from the sigmoid erythema."
    },
    {
      "id": "P12",
      "text": "1. Scalloped duodenal folds and antral erythema, biopsied."
    },
    {
      "id": "P13",
      "text": "2. Patchy sigmoid erythema, biopsied."
    }
  ],
